15.
Factors for determination of fee structure.
- The Fees Regulating Authority shall determine the reasonableness of the fee structure proposed by every unaided
institution, in respect of each professional course or group of courses, considering following factors :-
(i)
the location (Urban or Rural) of the institution;
(ii)
the cost of land and building ;
(iii)
minimum mandatorily required infrastructure or facilities, as specified by the appropriate authority ;
(iv)
the expenditure proposed or incurred on the facilities and amenities that are not mandatory as per the guidelines of the
appropriate authority ;
(v)
available number of qualified regularly appointed teaching and non-teaching staff as per the prescribed norms of the
appropriate authority ;
(vi)
expenses on the prescribed salaries of the teaching and non-teaching staff ;
(vii)
the expenditure on administration and the maintenance;
(viii)
the reasonable revenue surplus required for growth and development of the institution with particular reference to the
professional course conducted by it, which shall not be more than fifteen per cent. of educational revenue in the
